.TH mex 1 "2026-11-09" "mex" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
mex \- terminal UI to browse and debug mDNS/DNS-SD on the local link,
with anomaly detection

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mex
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Terminal UI to browse and debug mDNS/DNS-SD on the local link \(em live
services, records, queries, raw packets, and anomaly detection. Listens
passively on UDP port
5353 (IPv4 + IPv6 multicast) and also sends the standard browse queries
(service enumeration, PTR/SRV/TXT/A/AAAA). Suspicious records and
questions are flagged as anomalies, listed per service in the Anomalies
pane and in the metrics overlay.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-passive
Listen only: never transmit queries, just observe announcements.
With this flag mex transmits nothing: no startup QU batch, no continuous
queries, no TTL refreshes \(em the view shows recently heard traffic
decaying by TTL instead of actively maintained state.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interfaces \fIIFACES\fR
Network interfaces to use for mDNS discovery (e.g., br0, eth0).
Repeatable and comma-separated. Only the named links are joined, queried,
and ingested; unknown names abort at startup with the available list.
An explicit selection overrides the default loopback/container skip.
Without the flag, all usable links are browsed.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.

.SH LAYOUT
.TP
.B Hosts (left)
Collapsible tree grouped by hostname. Each header shows the service count
and primary address; each row shows the instance name with a short
service type and port. The selection is inverted, and the pane title always
names the selected row's host.
.TP
.B Answers (right top)
For the selected service: derived rows, then one row per observed raw
record with remaining TTL, flush bit, source, and rdata. Multi-pair TXT
records expand into unlabeled child rows. Records announced by this host
are highlighted; goodbye (TTL 0) records show as expired.
.TP
.B Questions (right middle)
Recently observed queries asking for the selected service, newest first,
with per-query age instead of TTL. Questions from this host are highlighted
like local records.
.TP
.B Anomalies (right, below Questions)
Every surfaced finding for the selected service, with the row's own
findings marked. Expired and goodbye rows name their state instead of
findings. Tab focuses it for scrolling; the pane follows the record
cursor.
.TP
.B Hex (right bottom)
Wire bytes of the selected record or question packet, falling back to the
service's latest packet. Tab focuses it for scrolling.
.TP
.B Mouse
Drag the shared pane borders to resize Hosts vs detail, and Answers /
Questions / Anomalies / Hex (the seam lights up). Click a row to
focus its pane and move the cursor there; clicking a host header folds it.
While mouse input is captured, use Shift+drag to select text in most
terminals.

.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Pane switching
.br
Tab / Shift+Tab      - Switch pane (Hosts \(-> Answers \(-> Questions \(-> Anomalies \(-> Hex)
.TP
.B Navigation
.br
Up/Down or j/k       - Move within the focused pane (scroll Hex when focused)
.br
h/l or \(<-/\(->         - Jump between host groups
.br
H/L                  - First / last host group
.br
Home/End             - First / last row of the focused pane (top / bottom of Hex)
.br
PageUp/PageDown or b/f or Space - Page (viewport scroll in Hex)
.br
Enter                - Fold / unfold host (Hosts) or TXT record (Answers)
.br
+/\-                  - Fold / unfold host (Hosts)
.br
*                    - Collapse all host groups / unfold all
.br
Ctrl+Up/Down, Ctrl+k, Shift+Up/Down, J/K - Scroll Answers viewport freely (Hex viewport when Hex focused)
.br
Ctrl+J                 - Dump mex state to JSON (experimental)
.TP
.B Other
.br
m                      - Metrics overlay (traffic, discovery, queries, links)
.br
j/k or Up/Down, h/l or \(<-/\(->, 0 - Scroll the overlay while open (vertical, horizontal, reset)
.br
q or Esc or Ctrl+C     - Quit (m / Esc closes the overlay first)
.br
Ctrl+Z (unix)          - Suspend to shell (fg resumes)
.br
Mouse drag on pane borders - Resize panes
.br
Mouse click            - Focus pane + move cursor (host header folds)
.br
Mouse wheel            - Move cursor one row / scroll one line (focused pane; overlay when open)

.SH ENVIRONMENT
Setting the NO_COLOR environment variable to any non-empty value (see https://no-color.org/) disables colors. The interface remains usable through text attributes such as reverse video for the selection.

.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu
Browse mDNS traffic:
.br
.B mex
.IP \(bu
Listen only, never transmit:
.br
.B mex \-\-passive
.IP \(bu
Browse only one link:
.br
.B mex \-i br0
.RE

